          "source_quote": "Οὐ δυσωπήσεις με περὶ τῆς οὐσίας αὐτοῦ σιωπή[σαν]τα περὶ τῆς προαιρέσεως αὐτοῦ [ζη]τεῖν μόνης.",
          "english_quote": "Will you not pressure me, after I have kept silent about his essence, to investigate only his purpose?",
          "issue": "The negative question changes Simon’s refusal into a question that ordinarily anticipates or invites pressure. The supplied edition prints a negative future declaration, and the following explanation that God’s essence can be discussed supports resistance to restricting the inquiry. The note’s assertion that the question form follows from οὐ is insufficient: οὐ does not itself establish interrogative force.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use a negative declaration, such as “You will not pressure me into keeping silent about his essence and investigating only his purpose.” Revise the accompanying note to explain the refusal and the relationship of σιωπήσαντα to ζητεῖν. Any replacement requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "19.12",
      "verdict": "accept",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
